      "writtenOn": "2026-11-01T19:00:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed with the check in `snd_pcm_mmap_data()`: it bounds the mapping by `vm_pgoff` only, so since aosp/4368055 an offset that isn\u0027t 16KB-aligned would make `remap_pfn_range()` (e.g. in `snd_dma_continuous_mmap()`) map up to 12KB past the buffer.\n\nI think this one isn\u0027t needed, though: on arm64, `pcm_status_mmap_allowed()` and `pcm_control_mmap_allowed()` are `false` (status and control mmaps are only built for x86, PPC and Alpha), so those offsets already fail with `-ENXIO` for every process, and every other offset goes to `snd_pcm_mmap_data()`.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this hunk? The shifted status case in `alsa_pcm_mmap_p3s` (aosp/4367986) would then get `-ENXIO`, as native processes do.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "7e1da6c74f452f162efd66a0d04d62bb2e55d606",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
